  "interpretation": "The signed error distribution is sharply peaked at zero and decays fast, and almost all remaining error is a single band in either direction. The subset that matters operationally is the tail that understates severity by two bands or more, because that is the case in which a reader is told the air is acceptable when it is not. Its size is reported above as an explicit safety statistic rather than being left implicit inside the macro-F1."
